This Western blot (Figure 7D) confirms that the IL-1β secreted by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) in the presence of Nano-11 and LPS priming is the active 17 kD form, rather than the inactive 30 kD pro-IL-1β. The blot shows pro-IL-1β in cell lysates with LPS treatment, while the active 17 kD IL-1β is detected in the supernatant only when BMDCs are treated with both LPS and Nano-11, indicating Nano-11's role in inducing the cleavage and secretion of this pro-inflammatory cytokine.